    {
      "id": "claim_b7ac7ab060f249269d9cd888b9fcd5ec",
      "statement": "The SDPA fallback has three paths: native is_causal SDPA for full-context equal-length inputs, key/value slicing to the last window+1 positions for single-token decode, and an explicit boolean mask offset by Tk - Tq with the window constraint for sliding-window training or chunked prefill.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://nanochat/flash_attention.py#L77-L112",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:57475daaf384e003cc20f6416716cff25c5e6a3c2cb4cdff69d680caca1f9026:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c24141e953924892bfaa3e3a81eda5d7",
      "statement": "In the KV-cache path the SDPA fallback mimics FA3's in-place cache update by reading the position from cache_seqlens[0] (assuming a uniform position across the batch), writing the new k/v into the cache, and attending over the cache prefix; neither backend advances cache_seqlens, which the model advances once after the last layer.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://nanochat/flash_attention.py#L139-L189",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:45a6f5eadfc95243c83697bb33fa651bec3b100abdc57005704ce8b3047b2b7b:"
